    "description": "ML Driven Imaging, Distributed Systems, Full Stack Workflow Engineering\n\n•\tDesigned and implemented a high throughput imaging and analysis pipeline integrating GPU staged data movement, zero copy shared memory IPC, and real time ML powered segmentation (YOLO/CUDA), enabling responsive visualization and downstream inference workflows.\n•\tRe architected the acquisition stack across Python and C++, eliminating lock contention and doubling throughput for ML adjacent imaging workloads.\n•\tBuilt a distributed, asynchronous persistence subsystem using worker thread pools, lock free queues, and cooperative work stealing, reducing end to end runtime and storage overhead by ~30% while supporting ML driven analysis stages.\n•\tDeveloped a cloud integrated workflow compiler translating JSON experiment metadata into executable pipelines using AWS Lambda, enabling scalable orchestration of ML adjacent processing steps.\n•\tContributed to full stack development of the experiment design platform, including backend services, data models, and Node.js/Electron UI components used to configure ML powered imaging and analysis workflows.\n•\tCreated the cell caging software system combining bitmap processing, geometry modeling, and GPU accelerated computer vision to support real time cell identification and downstream ML tasks.\n",
